# GreeterNameLabel: hover pill and pencil on the chosen person's name.
# NOTE: $TESSERA_BIN must point at the Rust binary. Name label position: centre of the screen area under the avatar (compare with the first shot, adjust the pointer path if the name sits elsewhere).
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo users &
wait 2
shot rest
note Glass greeter at rest: name with no pill and no pencil.
rec hover 1.2 ptr move 960 400 sleep 200 glide 960 480 300 sleep 800
note Pointer glided onto the name row: the soft pill fades in (about 150 ms) and a pencil (14 px) appears 6 px right of the name; opacity 0.8. Compare timing and size with QML.
# NOTE: the name position (960,480) is a guess for Glass; the reviewer should confirm that the pointer ends on the name.
shot hover
note Name hovered: pill background plus pencil visible to the right of the name; I-beam cursor not capturable.
rec leave 1.0 ptr move 960 480 sleep 200 glide 960 900 300 sleep 500
note Pointer left the name: pill and pencil fade out in about 150 ms.
# MANUAL: measure the 150 ms fade with anim-timing on the recordings
ptr move 960 480 sleep 200 click down up
# NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness
wait 0.6
shot clicked
note After a click on the name the username field replaces it with the name selected (same as QML).
key -k Escape
wait 0.5
key -k Escape
wait 1
# Material: name above the closed pill is inactive
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look material --demo users &
wait 2
shot m-closed
note Material, pill closed: the name above the pill is invisible and cannot be clicked (only the cookie and the closed pill with name show).
ptr move 960 540 sleep 200 glide 1000 600 300
wait 1
shot m-open
note After the pointer moved the pill opened and the name above it faded in; hover and click on it then work.
key -k Escape
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
